<title>USA: Arrow Air name GSAs for ex-Asia, Canada, Europe.</title>
<headline>Arrow Air name GSAs for ex-Asia, Canada, Europe.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>All-cargo airline Arrow Air has appointed new general sales agents in Asia and Canada.</p>
<p>The carrier said Pacific Express Co Ltd is assigned to develop new traffic from Asia to the South America and the Caribbean, with emphasis on Taiwan and Hong Kong as origin markets.</p>
<p>JAMP Interfreight Inc, will serve as GSA for Canada and will ship via truck to Miami to access the carrier's Caribbean and Latin American network.</p>
<p>Taipei-based Pacific Express will move goods to Arrow in Miami and Atlanta via interline arrangements with China Airlines and Northwest and via Panama City using EVA Air. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017 dg</p>
